---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'What is the CDMP certification?';
const description =
  'The Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP) is DAMA International’s globally recognised certification, based on the DMBOK. Here’s what it is, the levels, and how to prepare.';
const published = '2026-09-23';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: title,
  description,
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'DAMA South Africa',
    url: 'https://dama-south-africa.github.io/',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'DAMA South Africa',
    logo: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://dama-south-africa.github.io/logo.png',
    },
  },
  datePublished: published,
  dateModified: published,
  mainEntityOfPage:
    'https://dama-south-africa.github.io/resources/what-is-cdmp-certification/',
  inLanguage: 'en-ZA',
  about: 'CDMP certification, DAMA International, data management',
};
---

<Layout title={`${title} — DAMA South Africa`} description={description} jsonld={[article]}>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Resources</span>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="article-meta">By DAMA South Africa</p>
        <p class="lead">
          The Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP) is DAMA
          International&rsquo;s globally recognised certification for data
          management professionals. It is based on the DAMA Guide to the Data
          Management Body of Knowledge (DMBOK) and demonstrates rounded,
          tested competence across the discipline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What the CDMP measures</h2>
        <p>
          The CDMP is built on the DMBOK, the reference framework that defines
          the knowledge areas of data management — data governance, data
          architecture, data modelling and design, data quality, metadata,
          master and reference data, data integration, storage, security and
          more. Rather than testing one tool or platform, the CDMP checks that
          you understand how these areas work and fit together, which is why it
          is recognised across industries and countries.
        </p>

        <h2>The certification levels</h2>
        <p>
          Every CDMP candidate takes the same starting point, the
          <strong>CDMP Fundamentals exam</strong> — 100 multiple-choice
          questions drawn from across the DMBOK, in a 90-minute exam (with extra
          time available for English-second-language candidates). Your score on
          that exam, together with specialist exams, determines your level:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Associate</strong> — awarded on the Fundamentals exam alone,
            the entry point for those newer to the profession.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Practitioner</strong> — a stronger Fundamentals result plus
            <strong>two specialist exams</strong> in chosen knowledge areas,
            reflecting several years of practical experience.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Master</strong> — the highest examined level: a top
            Fundamentals result plus two specialist exams at the highest
            threshold, for senior, deeply experienced practitioners.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Specialist exams are available in areas such as Data Governance, Data
          Quality, Data Modelling &amp; Design, Metadata Management and Master
          &amp; Reference Data — so you can certify in the areas that match your
          work. For the current score thresholds and exam rules, always check
          the official CDMP site at
          <a href="https://cdmp.info/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cdmp.info</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it&rsquo;s worth it</h2>
        <p>
          For individuals, the CDMP is portable proof of data management
          competence that employers and clients recognise. For organisations,
          having certified people raises the standard of data work and gives a
          shared vocabulary rooted in the DMBOK. It is one of the few
          credentials that spans the whole discipline rather than a single
          niche.
        </p>

        <h2>How DAMA South Africa helps you prepare</h2>
        <p>
          As the local chapter of DAMA International, DAMA South Africa supports
          members working toward the CDMP with practical guidance and a
          <strong>weekly CDMP Q&amp;A webinar</strong> where you can ask
          questions and prepare for the exams. Formal, DMBOK-based training is
          delivered through our
          <a href="/training-providers/">registered training providers</a> —
          led by Modelware Systems, a DAMA International Registered Education
          Provider (REP) for CDMP certification.
        </p>
        <p>
          New to all of this? Start with our
          <a href="/resources/dmbok-knowledge-areas/">guide to the DMBOK
          knowledge areas</a>, learn more
          <a href="/about/">about the chapter</a>, or
          <a href="/become-a-member/">become a member</a> to join the community.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
